{
  "id": "terraform",
  "title": "Drift Detective",
  "coach": {
    "board": "Config, state and the real infrastructure sit side by side. A good day is all three agreeing.",
    "actions": "Next day ends the day, and drift lands overnight. Everything else you do in the terminal.",
    "firstMove": "Tap terraform, then init, then plan, and read what it says before you apply."
  },
  "healthLabel": "Team trust",
  "tickLabel": "Day",
  "manual": true,
  "stacked": true,
  "seed": 1,
  "schema": {
    "local_file": {
      "key": "filename",
      "forceNew": [],
      "data": false,
      "exists": "file already exists"
    },
    "aws_instance": {
      "key": null,
      "forceNew": [
        "ami"
      ],
      "data": false
    },
    "aws_s3_bucket": {
      "key": "bucket",
      "forceNew": [
        "bucket"
      ],
      "data": true,
      "exists": "BucketAlreadyOwnedByYou: Your previous request to create the named bucket succeeded and you already own it."
    },
    "aws_db_instance": {
      "key": "identifier",
      "forceNew": [
        "identifier",
        "engine"
      ],
      "data": true,
      "exists": "DBInstanceAlreadyExists: DB instance already exists"
    }
  },
  "events": [
    {
      "id": "var-change",
      "title": "A teammate changed a variable",
      "fix": "A changed input shows up on the next plan as `~` update in-place. Read the plan, then apply it in the workspace the change is meant for.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/01-core-workflow.md",
        "section": "Try it: `examples/local-file`"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "console-edit",
      "title": "Someone edited a resource by hand in the console",
      "fix": "plan refreshes state against reality and proposes to undo the manual change. Apply to revert it, or edit the config to match if the change was wanted.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/01-core-workflow.md",
        "section": "State"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hand-made",
      "title": "A teammate created a resource by hand and wrote its config",
      "fix": "A create fails if the object already exists. `terraform import ADDRESS ID` records the existing object in state, and the next plan shows only what differs.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/01-core-workflow.md",
        "section": "State"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "forces-replace",
      "title": "A config change would replace the database",
      "fix": "`-/+` with `# forces replacement` means destroy, then create. For a database that is data loss. Read every plan: revert the change, or plan a migration.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/01-core-workflow.md",
        "section": "Core workflow"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "data-loss",
      "title": "Terraform destroyed a stateful resource",
      "fix": "A forced replacement or a destroy deletes the data with it. Plans exist so you read `-/+` and `-` lines before you type yes.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/01-core-workflow.md",
        "section": "Core workflow"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lock-active",
      "title": "CI is holding the state lock",
      "fix": "A lock means an operation is in flight. Wait for it to finish; forcing the lock open while it runs puts two writers on one state.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/03-state-and-workspaces.md",
        "section": "Drift and locking, in practice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lock-stale",
      "title": "A crashed CI job left the state locked",
      "fix": "Confirm nothing is really running (check the pipeline), then `terraform force-unlock LOCK_ID` with the ID from the error.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/03-state-and-workspaces.md",
        "section": "Drift and locking, in practice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lock-forced",
      "title": "You forced a lock that was still held",
      "fix": "The running job lost its lock and can now write over your changes. Only force-unlock after confirming no apply is in flight.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/03-state-and-workspaces.md",
        "section": "Drift and locking, in practice"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "state-lost",
      "title": "A laptop was reimaged: terraform.tfstate is gone",
      "fix": "Local state lives on one machine. Remote state survives it; without it Terraform forgets what it manages, and every create collides with the object that already exists.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/03-state-and-workspaces.md",
        "section": "Why remote state"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "module-extracted",
      "title": "The refactoring changed every resource address",
      "fix": "Terraform tracks resources by address, so a resource that moves into a module looks like one destroyed and one created. Tell it the object moved, with a `moved` block or `terraform state mv`, instead of letting it destroy and recreate.",
      "learn": {
        "note": "topics/terraform/notes/02-variables-and-modules.md",
        "section": "Refactoring into a module"
      }
    }
  ],
  "levels": [
    {
      "id": "first-apply",
      "title": "1. First apply",
      "blurb": "The workflow from topics/terraform/examples/local-file: init, plan, apply. Then a teammate changes a variable and someone edits the file by hand. Read each plan before you apply.",
      "hints": [
        "Look at the state panel: nothing is managed until you init and apply.",
        "A plan shows what will change before you apply it. After the first apply, changes arrive from outside.",
        "terraform init, terraform apply -auto-approve; then press Next day and apply again whenever the plan shows a difference."
      ],
      "par": 3,
      "winTicks": 4,
      "minHealth": 50,
      "workspace": "default",
      "initialized": false,
      "stateStore": "local",
      "config": {
        "backend": false,
        "vars": {
          "greeting": "hello from the cookbook"
        },
        "resources": {
          "local_file.greeting": {
            "type": "local_file",
            "attrs": {
              "content": {
                "var": "greeting"
              },
              "filename": "greeting.txt"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "envs": {
        "default": {
          "deployed": []
        }
      },
      "schedule": [
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "event": "var-change",
          "var": "greeting",
          "value": "hi from the team"
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "event": "console-edit",
          "env": "default",
          "addr": "local_file.greeting",
          "attr": "content",
          "value": "oops, edited by hand"
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform init"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "nextDay"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "drift",
      "title": "2. Drift and imports",
      "blurb": "An instance, a bucket and a database are running. Reality will move without Terraform, and a teammate will make a change that looks harmless in the diff. Keep config, state and reality in agreement without destroying data.",
      "hints": [
        "Look at the state and real infrastructure panels side by side: anything real but missing from state is drift.",
        "A bucket was made outside Terraform and needs importing, and a rename that looks harmless would destroy and recreate the database.",
        "Apply what the plan shows, import aws_s3_bucket.assets acme-assets, and set the identifier back to orders-db so the plan stays empty."
      ],
      "par": 4,
      "winTicks": 5,
      "minHealth": 50,
      "workspace": "default",
      "initialized": true,
      "stateStore": "local",
      "config": {
        "backend": false,
        "vars": {},
        "resources": {
          "aws_instance.web": {
            "type": "aws_instance",
            "attrs": {
              "ami": "ami-0abc123",
              "instance_type": "t3.micro"
            }
          },
          "aws_s3_bucket.logs": {
            "type": "aws_s3_bucket",
            "attrs": {
              "bucket": "acme-logs",
              "versioning": "Enabled"
            }
          },
          "aws_db_instance.main": {
            "type": "aws_db_instance",
            "attrs": {
              "identifier": "orders-db",
              "engine": "postgres",
              "instance_class": "db.t3.micro"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "envs": {
        "default": {
          "deployed": [
            "aws_instance.web",
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs",
            "aws_db_instance.main"
          ]
        }
      },
      "schedule": [
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "event": "console-edit",
          "env": "default",
          "addr": "aws_instance.web",
          "attr": "instance_type",
          "value": "t3.large"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "event": "hand-made",
          "env": "default",
          "addr": "aws_s3_bucket.assets",
          "id": "acme-assets",
          "type": "aws_s3_bucket",
          "attrs": {
            "bucket": "acme-assets",
            "versioning": "Disabled"
          },
          "config": {
            "bucket": "acme-assets",
            "versioning": "Enabled"
          }
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "event": "forces-replace",
          "addr": "aws_db_instance.main",
          "attr": "identifier",
          "value": "orders-db-v2"
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform import aws_s3_bucket.assets acme-assets"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "setAttr",
          "args": [
            "aws_db_instance.main",
            "identifier",
            "orders-db"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "action": "nextDay"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "team",
      "title": "3. Team chaos",
      "blurb": "Two workspaces, dev and prod, and a teammate who just added a remote backend block. CI shares your state, locks come and go, and you start in prod. Check which workspace you are in before every plan.",
      "hints": [
        "Check the workspace in the status strip before every plan: you start in prod.",
        "The new backend block needs a state migration, and a stale lock blocks you until it is released.",
        "terraform init -migrate-state, select dev before applying, then prod; for a stale lock, force-unlock with the ID the error prints."
      ],
      "par": 4,
      "winTicks": 6,
      "minHealth": 50,
      "workspace": "prod",
      "initialized": false,
      "stateStore": "local",
      "config": {
        "backend": true,
        "vars": {
          "size": "t3.micro"
        },
        "resources": {
          "aws_instance.web": {
            "type": "aws_instance",
            "attrs": {
              "ami": "ami-0abc123",
              "instance_type": {
                "ws": {
                  "prod": "m5.large",
                  "*": {
                    "var": "size"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "aws_s3_bucket.logs": {
            "type": "aws_s3_bucket",
            "attrs": {
              "bucket": {
                "ws": {
                  "prod": "acme-prod-logs",
                  "*": "acme-dev-logs"
                }
              },
              "versioning": "Enabled"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "envs": {
        "dev": {
          "deployed": [
            "aws_instance.web",
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs"
          ]
        },
        "prod": {
          "deployed": [
            "aws_instance.web",
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs"
          ]
        }
      },
      "schedule": [
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "event": "var-change",
          "var": "size",
          "value": "t3.small"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "event": "console-edit",
          "env": "prod",
          "addr": "aws_instance.web",
          "attr": "instance_type",
          "value": "m5.2xlarge"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "event": "lock-active",
          "lockId": "6a4e2f1c-9b1d-4c33-8f0a-2d5e7b9c1a10",
          "who": "ci-runner@nightly-plan",
          "op": "OperationTypePlan",
          "days": 1
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "event": "state-lost"
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "event": "console-edit",
          "env": "dev",
          "addr": "aws_s3_bucket.logs",
          "attr": "versioning",
          "value": "Suspended"
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "event": "lock-stale",
          "lockId": "b81c0d52-7e44-4a0f-9d3b-5c2a8e6f1b77",
          "who": "ci-runner@deploy-812",
          "op": "OperationTypeApply"
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform init -migrate-state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform workspace select dev"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform workspace select prod"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 3,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform force-unlock b81c0d52-7e44-4a0f-9d3b-5c2a8e6f1b77"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform workspace select dev"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 4,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 5,
          "action": "nextDay"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "module",
      "title": "4. Copy-paste to module",
      "blurb": "Two stacks (an instance and a log bucket each) are copy-pasted in main.tf. Extract them into a module without touching the real infrastructure: read the plan after you extract, and make Terraform move the state instead of destroying the buckets.",
      "hints": [
        "Look at main.tf: the two stacks are the same code pasted twice.",
        "Moving code into a module changes the resource addresses, so Terraform would destroy and recreate; a moved block says the old address is the new one.",
        "Extract the module, add a moved entry for each of the four resources, then apply and check the plan touches nothing real."
      ],
      "par": 6,
      "winTicks": 3,
      "minHealth": 50,
      "nagCost": 3,
      "workspace": "default",
      "initialized": true,
      "stateStore": "local",
      "config": {
        "backend": false,
        "vars": {},
        "resources": {
          "aws_instance.web_a": {
            "type": "aws_instance",
            "attrs": {
              "ami": "ami-0abc123",
              "instance_type": "t3.micro",
              "name": "svc-a-web"
            }
          },
          "aws_s3_bucket.logs_a": {
            "type": "aws_s3_bucket",
            "attrs": {
              "bucket": "acme-a-logs",
              "versioning": "Enabled"
            }
          },
          "aws_instance.web_b": {
            "type": "aws_instance",
            "attrs": {
              "ami": "ami-0abc123",
              "instance_type": "t3.micro",
              "name": "svc-b-web"
            }
          },
          "aws_s3_bucket.logs_b": {
            "type": "aws_s3_bucket",
            "attrs": {
              "bucket": "acme-b-logs",
              "versioning": "Enabled"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "envs": {
        "default": {
          "deployed": [
            "aws_instance.web_a",
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs_a",
            "aws_instance.web_b",
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs_b"
          ]
        }
      },
      "refactor": {
        "module": "service",
        "mapping": [
          {
            "from": "aws_instance.web_a",
            "to": "module.svc_a.aws_instance.web"
          },
          {
            "from": "aws_s3_bucket.logs_a",
            "to": "module.svc_a.aws_s3_bucket.logs"
          },
          {
            "from": "aws_instance.web_b",
            "to": "module.svc_b.aws_instance.web"
          },
          {
            "from": "aws_s3_bucket.logs_b",
            "to": "module.svc_b.aws_s3_bucket.logs"
          }
        ],
        "configText": [
          "module \"svc_a\" {",
          "  source = \"./modules/service\"",
          "  name   = \"svc-a\"",
          "}",
          "",
          "module \"svc_b\" {",
          "  source = \"./modules/service\"",
          "  name   = \"svc-b\"",
          "}",
          "",
          "# modules/service/main.tf",
          "resource \"aws_instance\" \"web\" {",
          "  ami           = \"ami-0abc123\"",
          "  instance_type = \"t3.micro\"",
          "  name          = \"${var.name}-web\"",
          "}",
          "",
          "resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"logs\" {",
          "  bucket     = \"acme-${trimprefix(var.name, \"svc-\")}-logs\"",
          "  versioning = \"Enabled\"",
          "}"
        ]
      },
      "schedule": [],
      "solution": [
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "extractModule"
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "addMoved",
          "args": [
            "aws_instance.web_a",
            "module.svc_a.aws_instance.web"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "addMoved",
          "args": [
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs_a",
            "module.svc_a.aws_s3_bucket.logs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "addMoved",
          "args": [
            "aws_instance.web_b",
            "module.svc_b.aws_instance.web"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "addMoved",
          "args": [
            "aws_s3_bucket.logs_b",
            "module.svc_b.aws_s3_bucket.logs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "terraform",
          "args": [
            "terraform apply -auto-approve"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tick": 0,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 1,
          "action": "nextDay"
        },
        {
          "tick": 2,
          "action": "nextDay"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
